(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - NITI AAYOG) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: ATAL INNOVATION MISSION - SEED & INCUBATION SUPPORT \(AIM\) / ATAL INNOVATION MISSION \(AIM\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(Catalyzes world-class startups through Atal Incubation Centres \(AICs\) with) Tj
T*
(prototyping labs, maker spaces, and access to seed grants.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. Innovators and early-stage ventures working on technology, circular) Tj
T*
(   economy, rural development, or high-impact social solutions.) Tj
T*
(2. Must apply to and be shortlisted by an Atal Incubation Centre \(AIC\) or) Tj
T*
(   Established Incubation Centre \(EIC\).) Tj
T*
(3. Clear intent to incorporate a commercial enterprise in India.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. Incubation access, state-of-the-art laboratory infrastructure, corporate) Tj
T*
(   POCs, and micro seed grants ranging from Rs. 5 Lakh to Rs. 25 Lakh.) Tj
T*
(3. Maximum financial assistance cap is Rs 25.0 Lakh per unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. Business Pitch Deck) Tj
T*
(2. Prototype demonstrations or design schematics) Tj
T*
(3. Founding team credentials) Tj
T*
(4. GST / ROC registration if incorporated) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Online via Atal Innovation Mission Portal or respective AIC websites) Tj
T*
(2. Official Portal: https://aim.gov.in/) Tj
T*
ET
